  },
  "notes": [
    {
      "section": "Styles",
      "topic": "class-dependent rules inside a shared section",
      "note": "The default entry's Styles section has declarations the classless entries lack: --femto-grid-column-gap and --femto-grid-row-gap in the first :root, :host block; 'a.secondary, a.contrast { --femto-text-decoration: underline }'; 'details.dropdown summary:not([role=button])' and 'nav details.dropdown summary:focus-visible' (--femto-outline-width); and two '[role=search]:has(... .secondary:focus ...), [role=group]:has(...)' and '.contrast' rules (--femto-group-box-shadow-focus-with-button). If tokens/base.css or layout/elements.css is shared by every entry, these must move to classes/* files (default only), which moves them later in the cascade, or classless gains them."
    },
    {
      "section": "Styles",
      "topic": "selectors that differ between entries",
      "note": "Default writes 'details summary[role=button]:not(.outline)::after' and '[aria-busy=true]:not(input, select, textarea):is(button, [type=submit], [type=button], [type=reset], [role=button]):not(.outline)::before' (filter: brightness(0) invert(1)); classless writes the same selectors without ':not(.outline)', so they have one class less specificity. One shared file cannot match both; using the default selector in classless raises specificity there."
    },
    {
      "section": "Styles",
      "topic": "theme-color-dependent declaration outside Color schemes",
      "note": "For the six light-primary themes (amber, grey, lime, pumpkin, sand, yellow; --femto-primary-inverse: #000) the Styles rule '[aria-busy=true]...:not(.outline)::before' becomes 'filter: brightness(0) invert(0)' instead of invert(1), in both femto.<color>.css and femto.classless.<color>.css. The neighbouring 'details summary[role=button]:not(.outline)::after' keeps invert(1) in every theme (a 2.1.1 inconsistency to keep). So themes/<color>.css for those six must override one declaration from the Styles section, not only scheme tokens. This is the 28th theme-dependent declaration counted in PLAN."
    },
    {
      "section": "Styles",
      "topic": "where the option references change Styles",
      "note": "Both responsive options live in the Styles section: options/femto.fixed-typography.css drops the five '@media (min-width: ...) { :root, :host { --femto-font-size: ... } }' blocks right after the first :root block; options/femto.responsive-spacings.css inserts five media blocks for 'body > header, body > main, body > footer, section' and five for 'article' (--femto-block-spacing-vertical/horizontal) at the same place. An appended options/*.css file sits at the end of the cascade instead; the hybrid build will show whether that order matters."
    },
    {
      "section": "Color schemes",
      "topic": "theme-color-dependent declarations",
      "note": "Every non-azure theme changes 7 tokens in each of the 3 scheme blocks (light; media dark; [data-theme=dark]): --femto-text-selection-color, --femto-primary, --femto-primary-background, --femto-primary-underline, --femto-primary-hover, --femto-primary-hover-background, --femto-primary-focus (21 declarations). The six light-primary themes also change --femto-primary-inverse (#fff -> #000) and --femto-switch-thumb-box-shadow (0 0 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0) -> 0 0 0.5rem rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25)) in each block (6 more), plus the Styles filter above: 28 in all. No other section depends on the theme color."
    },
    {
      "section": "Color schemes",
      "topic": "class-dependent declarations",
      "note": "Default only: five --femto-dropdown-* tokens (background-color, border-color, box-shadow, color, hover-background-color) in each scheme block, and in both dark blocks 'details summary[role=button].contrast:not(.outline)::after' and '[aria-busy=true]...contrast...:not(.outline)::before' { filter: brightness(0) }. These belong with classes/dropdown.css and classes/buttons.css (or a classes/ schemes file), not tokens/schemes.css, if classless must not gain them."
    },
    {
      "section": "Color schemes",
      "topic": "scheme selectors differ from the PLAN snippet",
      "note": "2.1.1 writes the light block as '[data-theme=light], :root:not([data-theme=dark]), :host(:not([data-theme=dark]))', the dark media block as '@media only screen and (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { :root:not([data-theme]), :host(:not([data-theme])) }', and '[data-theme=dark]'. The PLAN 'Light and dark' snippet omits both :host() forms and 'only screen and'. Without 'only screen', print output with a dark OS preference turns dark where 2.1.1 stays light; without :host(), shadow roots lose their scheme."
    },
    {
      "section": "Color schemes",
      "topic": "non-token rules in the section",
      "note": "Besides the three token blocks the section has, per scheme, 'input:is([type=submit], [type=button], [type=reset], [type=checkbox], [type=radio], [type=file])' { --femto-form-element-focus-color: var(--femto-primary-focus) } under each scheme selector, the --femto-icon-valid and --femto-icon-invalid data-URI tokens, which stay per scheme, and at its very end an unscoped 'progress, [type=checkbox], [type=radio], [type=range] { accent-color: var(--femto-primary) }'."
    },
    {
      "section": "Landmarks",
      "topic": "entries differ structurally",
      "note": "Default: 'body > header, body > main, body > footer { padding-block: var(--femto-block-spacing-vertical) }'. Classless replaces that rule with '{ width: 100%; margin-right: auto; margin-left: auto; padding: var(--femto-block-spacing-vertical) var(--femto-block-spacing-horizontal) }' plus five viewport media blocks (max-width 510/700/950/1200/1450px; padding-right/left 0 from 576px). Fluid classless is classless without those five media blocks; that is the only difference between femto.classless.css and femto.fluid.classless.css. An appended options/fluid.css must therefore cancel max-width and restore the horizontal padding from 576px up, or the fluid entry needs a different landmarks-container file."
    },
    {
      "section": "Container, Grid, Overflow auto, Dropdown (details.dropdown)",
      "topic": "sections missing from classless",
      "note": "The classless and fluid-classless references have no Container, Grid, Overflow auto or Dropdown banner at all (30 banners against 34)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Link, Button, Modal (<dialog>)",
      "topic": "class rules in the middle of a section",
      "note": "Link: the .secondary and .contrast rules sit before 'a[role=button] { display: inline-block }'. Button: .secondary, .contrast and .outline rules are interleaved with element rules. Modal: '.close' is merged into the same selector lists as ':is(a, button)[rel=prev]' (3 rules), and .modal-is-open, .modal-is-opening/.modal-is-closing and the modal-overlay and modal keyframes are default only. Appending classes/*.css after the content file reorders these rules; classes/modal.css has to repeat the rel=prev declarations under '.close' selectors."
    },
    {
      "section": "Button",
      "topic": "selector list that differs between entries",
      "note": "Default's secondary focus rule lists '[type=reset]:focus, [type=reset]:is([aria-current]:not([aria-current=false])):focus, [type=file]::file-selector-button:focus, [type=file]::file-selector-button:is([aria-current]:not([aria-current=false])):focus'; classless lists only '[type=reset]:focus, [type=file]::file-selector-button:focus'. Sharing the default list gives a focused reset button with aria-current the secondary focus ring in classless, where 2.1.1 classless shows the primary one (a registrable natural fix)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Basics form elements",
      "topic": "class inside :where()",
      "note": "Default writes ':where(input, select, textarea, fieldset, .grid) + small' and the [aria-invalid=false] and [aria-invalid=true] forms; classless drops '.grid'. :where() has zero specificity, so sharing the default selectors only changes classless pages that use class=\"grid\"."
    },
    {
      "section": "Table",
      "topic": "classless ships table.striped",
      "note": "femto.classless.css and femto.fluid.classless.css contain 'table.striped' rules (a 2.1.1 bug); the draft map omits classes/table-striped.css from classless, which is the registered natural fix in PLAN."
    },
    {
      "section": "(all)",
      "topic": "theme references",
      "note": "css/pico.<color>.css and css/pico.classless.<color>.css came from scripts/build-themes.js (sass.compile, whose 'outputStyle' option is ignored, so the output is expanded) and, unlike the three entry files, end without a trailing newline. Their banners match their entry exactly."
    },
    {
      "section": "(options)",
      "topic": "no-transitions reference removes more than durations",
      "note": "$enable-transitions: false keeps '--femto-transition: 0.2s ease-in-out' defined but drops every 'transition' declaration (including the -webkit-/-moz-/-ms- copies in the range track and thumb and progress pseudo-element rules, and the switch thumb's 'transition: margin 0.1s ease-in-out'), the modal animation rules (.modal-is-opening/.modal-is-closing) with the modal-overlay and modal keyframes, and every tooltip slide animation with its keyframes and --femto-tooltip-slide-to/--femto-tooltip-caret-slide-to tokens. An options/no-transitions.css that only sets '--femto-transition: 0s' leaves transition-property lists, modal animations and tooltip animations in place, so those show up as differences."
    }
  ]
}
